Z||000002||BlackGT||03-05-2000||01:29 AM||||Well folks....here goes nothing! I`m going to attempt to replace my clutch in a friend`s garage. 1FST2M6 explained the details of the <BR>job but like everything else with a Fiero it<BR>won`t be easy. This is coming from a non-backyard mechanic who is slowly but surely becoming one because of this obsession<BR>with this little GO-KART for the street! I love this car and it pains my greatly to see<BR>"Misty" down with clutch woes but with a little luck and some help we`ll be able to <BR>live up to my tag with says: "CMEFLY"<BR>Wish me luck!||||reg||14
Z||000003||BlackGT||03-06-2000||11:38 PM||||Well folks here`s an update on my clutch replacement............after a day and a half <BR>I`m not done! While trying to free stuck bolts I ask myself what have I gotten myself into? Right now my beloved baby is sitting on<BR>jack stands with the rear cradle bolts out, brake calipers hangin, suspension only held in place by the A arms trying to figure out<BR>which bolts to try to remove to get the transaxle out and in the open so I can have<BR>the flywheel turned and replace the rear main seal, clutch disc and the pressure plate. Maybe I`ll be able to get this together tomorrow so I can drive. This is my only means of tranportation so I`m really under<BR>pressure to finish what I`ve started. After<BR>reading Ed Parks procedure for this and comparing it with 1FST2M6`s way I`m left<BR>scratching my head and muttering to myself!<BR>I truly understand why automotive technicians get paid as much as they do. This is the biggest job on a car that I`ve ever attempted<BR>to do and after this I won`t be so eager to<BR>try again without someone who knows what they`re doing assisting! It`s after 11:00<BR>so I`m going to call it a day.....hopefully<BR>tomorrow will be a sucess and I`ll be back on the road....wish me luck!!!!!||||reg||9
Z||000004||Phaeton||03-07-2000||02:25 AM||||Good Luck!  My first Fiero clutch took sixteen hours in a GM dealer's fully equipped shop.  All kinds of fancy equipment, just a singular lack of intimate Fiero knowledge. ||||reg||12
Z||000005||Raydar||03-09-2000||10:10 PM||||Good luck, Todd. Be careful, eh? ||||reg||1
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||03-10-2000||12:33 AM||||I did the same thing... Laying under my Fiero with bloody knuckles, oil on my face, fire in my eyes and nasty words on my tongue. Just keep plugging away at it and it will all be worth it. Just think, when you're standing around the watercooler at work, instead of saying "I sat around this weekend" you can say "I replaced the clutch in my car." <P>How's it going? Done yet?||||reg||1
